      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2011. Published by Elsevier SAS.",
        "AbstractText": "We report a case of an acute pancreatitis complicated by myocardial infarction with normal coronary arteries on angiography. This observation presents a double interest. First, it illustrates unusual forms of coronary disease represented by the non-atherosclerotic infarction. On the other hand, it shows that the multiple visceral damage associated with acute pancreatitis can include myocardial infarction which complications aggravate prognosis."
      },
